  "summary": "A 404 Media newsletter highlights leaked audio from Flock CEO Garrett Langley at the IACP conference in Orlando, where he claimed anti-Flock protests are not organic but driven by Russian bots. The piece references ongoing community backlash and contract cancellations, including a DeFlock rally in Norfolk, Virginia.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Garrett Langley, the CEO of automatic license plate reader company Flock, told an audience of police chiefs at a private police conference Sunday that anti-Flock protests around the country are not real, according to leaked audio obtained by 404 Media.",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "It's anonymous bots, and so it is not real",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "Langley made the comments at the International Association of Chiefs of Police (IACP) conference, which is running Saturday to Tuesday in Orlando, Florida.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
  ],
